Start the named shared services, or all of them, and reconnect every worktree
that uses them. A service that is already running is left alone: one whose
definition differs from this worktree's is refused unless you pass --recreate
with its name, which replaces that service with this worktree's definition and
keeps its data. This is also how a worktree left unconnected, by a busy lock or
a daemon restart, is repaired.

Usage:
  treerig shared up [name...] [flags]

Flags:
      --config string                 path to treerig.toml (default: nearest
                                      above cwd)
  -h, --help                          help for up
      --reallocate-port stringArray   move a container port to a new loopback
                                      port, as <name>:<container port>; refused
                                      while the service runs (repeatable)
      --recreate                      replace running services with this
                                      worktree's definition, keeping their data

Global Flags:
      --progress mode   how to show progress: auto (redraw on a terminal) or
                        plain (one line per change) (default "auto")
  -v, --verbose         show what treerig runs, and every detail
